@startuml
title Fluxo Simples de Login: Cliente -> API Node.js -> PostgreSQL -> JWT
autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Cliente\n(Web / Mobile)" as Client
participant "API Node.js\n(Express / Fastify)" as API
database "PostgreSQL\n(Tabela users)" as DB
participant "Módulo JWT\n(jsonwebtoken)" as JWT

Client -> API : POST /login\n{ "email": "dev@empresa.com", "password": "***" }
activate API

API -> DB : SELECT id, email, password_hash\nFROM users WHERE email = $1
activate DB
DB --> API : Retorna registro do usuário (ou null)
deactivate DB

API -> API : Valida hash da senha\nbcrypt.compare(password, user.password_hash)

alt Usuário existe E senha confere
    API -> JWT : jwt.sign({ sub: user.id, email: user.email }, JWT_SECRET, { expiresIn: '1h' })
    activate JWT
    JWT --> API : Retorna token assinado (header.payload.signature)
    deactivate JWT

    API --> Client : HTTP 200 OK\n{ "accessToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIs..." }
else Usuário não encontrado OU senha incorreta
    API --> Client : HTTP 401 Unauthorized\n{ "error": "Credenciais inválidas" }
end

deactivate API
@enduml
